Terminal owns a Process and a text input field for the generic inspector.
initialize creates the Process and empty input.
process returns the underlying Process; environment: configures its inherited environment overrides before launch.
start:args:cwd: launches the executable and literal argument Array in a new 80-column, 24-row terminal, returning self.
write: sends exact text bytes and returns bytes written; sendLine: adds a newline.
read drains this terminal's bounded unread text. output returns recent terminal output. droppedBytes reports unread bytes discarded by the bound.
readFrom: accepts a nonnegative byte offset and returns a JSON TerminalReadResponse without consuming another reader's output.
resizeColumns:rows: changes the live terminal dimensions, each an integer from 1 through 65535.
status, exitCode, error, command and pid describe the child. wait returns its final exit code.
signal: addresses the terminal process group. interrupt writes the terminal interrupt character. stop kills the terminal process group.
input and input: support the generic editable input field; sendInput sends that field as a line.
inspectorMetadata describes editable arguments and status properties. inspectorViews offers output, input, send, interrupt and stop controls.
